From 804652125f04f010e547c14f97c1da6c8f600b67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 09:16:05 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] rpc(v2): process native PSBTs through explicit version
 dispatch

Dispatch native documents before legacy PSBT parsing. Reject v7 unsigned-tx wrappers and unsafe signature-discard overrides, authenticate updates with full local SMT coins, and reuse existing wallet compressed keys for supported native slots. Extraction verifies ordinary native validation plus current node transaction/input/script checks; partial modes require explicit matching authorization.

Add disconnected two-node native-keyhash PSBT exchange, identity/metadata preservation and rejection controls. Existing legacy PSBT creator and transaction formats retain their v0 path. Native coin selection, descriptor import, bridge automation and Bitcoin hardware-wallet compatibility are not claimed. Normal daemon build and functional before/after validation pending coordinated resource slots.
